#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This tutorial is inspired by and based upon research conducted at Cleveland Clinic, as described in [Kaliakin, Danil, et al. \"Implicit solvent sample-based quantum diagonalization.\" The Journal of Physical Chemistry B 129.23 (2025): 5788-5796](https://pubs.acs.org/doi/10.1021/acs.jpcb.5c01030), exposing the full workflow for implicit solvent calculations and extending it with iterative solvent self-consistency (\"The Heartwood Algorithm\", M. Motta, T. Pellegrini, 2025), geometry optimization, and automatic qubit layout selection. Please refer to the [SQD IEF-PCM Qiskit Function template](/guides/function-template-chemistry-workflow), jointly developed by Cleveland Clinic and IBM&reg; based on Cleveland Clinic research, for a streamlined, black-box interface for running implicit solvent calculations.\n"
msgstr "Questo tutorial è ispirato e basato sulla ricerca condotta presso la Cleveland Clinic, come descritto in [Kaliakin, Danil, et al. \"Implicit solvent sample-based quantum diagonalization.\" The Journal of Physical Chemistry B 129.23 (2025): 5788-5796](https://pubs.acs.org/doi/10.1021/acs.jpcb.5c01030), che espone il flusso di lavoro completo per i calcoli con solvente implicito ed lo estende con l'auto-consistenza iterativa del solvente (\"The Heartwood Algorithm\", M. Motta, T. Pellegrini, 2025), l'ottimizzazione della geometria, e la selezione automatica del layout dei qubit. Fai riferimento al [modello di funzione Qiskit SQD IEF-PCM](/guides/function-template-chemistry-workflow), sviluppato congiuntamente da Cleveland Clinic e IBM&reg; sulla base della ricerca di Cleveland Clinic, per un'interfaccia black-box semplificata per eseguire calcoli con solvente implicito.\n"

